capability md/tables  GFM tables, with their column alignments
  heroes  markdown.Options.tables, markdown.Node, markdown.Align
  go      extension.Table, extension.NewTable, extension.NewTableParser, extension.NewTableHTMLRenderer, extension.NewTableASTTransformer, extension.NewTableParagraphTransformer, extension.TableConfig, extension.TableOption, extension.TableCellAlignMethod, extension.TableHTMLRenderer, extension.TableAttributeFilter, extension.TableHeaderAttributeFilter, extension.TableRowAttributeFilter, extension.TableThCellAttributeFilter, extension.TableTdCellAttributeFilter
  rust    pulldown_cmark::Options::ENABLE_TABLES, comrak::ExtensionOptions.table
  python  MarkdownIt.enable
  note    a delimiter row turns the paragraph's last line into a header, the lines before it staying a paragraph (GFM's examples do not settle a paragraph of several lines; cmark-gfm was not asked); a row shorter than the header is filled, a longer one cut; `align="..."` on each cell

