  python  MarkdownIt.enable
  note    an opener and a closer of the same length, one or two tildes; three or more are text

capability md/autolinks  GFM's extended autolinks: `www.`, `http://`, `https://`, `ftp://` and email addresses without `<` and `>`
  heroes  markdown.Options.autolinks
  go      extension.Linkify, extension.NewLinkify, extension.NewLinkifyParser, extension.LinkifyConfig, extension.LinkifyOption
  rust    comrak::ExtensionOptions.autolink, comrak::ParseOptions.relaxed_autolinks
  python  -
  note    found in text after reading, never inside a link, by the GFM specification's rules: valid domains, trailing punctuation, unbalanced parentheses and entity-like endings left out. comrak's relaxed autolinks, another rule, are not taken

capability md/task-lists  GFM task list items, `- [ ]` and `- [x]`
  heroes  markdown.Options.task_lists, markdown.Task
  go      extension.TaskList, extension.NewTaskCheckBoxParser, extension.NewTaskCheckBoxHTMLRenderer, extension.TaskCheckBoxHTMLRenderer
  rust    pulldown_cmark::Options::ENABLE_TASKLISTS, comrak::ExtensionOptions.tasklist, comrak::ParseOptions.relaxed_tasklist_matching, comrak::RenderOptions.tasklist_classes
  python  -
  note    written as GFM's examples write them, `<input disabled="" type="checkbox">`; a box is `[ ]`, `[x]` or `[X]` before a space or a tab, as GFM reads it

capability md/raw-html  raw HTML escaped, or kept
  heroes  markdown.Options.keep_html
  go      renderer/html.WithUnsafe
  rust    comrak::RenderOptions.unsafe_, comrak::RenderOptions.escape
  python  MarkdownIt
  note    escaped by default, so that it shows as text, an HTML block inside `<p>`; kept, it is written as the reference writes it. What the other libraries do by default was not asked

